      "purposeInStoryline": "Lesson 2 showed that actual income was KES 2,630 below the plan and that the '10% OFF' sign was involved. This lesson calculates the discounts and shows that they account for KES 2,000 of that gap. The remaining KES 630 is left for Lesson 4 (commission). Learners also see why a seller offers a discount, which starts to answer the second key inquiry question.",
      "safetyNotes": "No specific hazards. Role-play money is paper cards or counters; do not use real money. Keep movement around the classroom orderly."
