        "teacherMoves": "Display the formulas: Commission = rate % x sales; % commission = commission / sales x 100. Model the first calculation aloud: \"First I write 5 over 100, then multiply by 12,600.\" Ask: \"Why do we use 12,600 and not the marked-price total of 14,000?\" WAIT TIME 10 seconds, then cold-call 3 learners. Circulate during group work and cold-call 2 groups to show their 8% working. Ask: \"Is commission paid on the cost price or on the sales value?\" Point out that all figures are illustrative.",
