      "knowledge": "• Profit = selling price - cost price; loss = cost price - selling price.\n• Percentage profit or loss = profit or loss / cost price x 100, always on the COST price.\n• The stall's profit on stock was KES 3,600 (25% of KES 14,400). After commission (KES 630) and stall costs (KES 600) the net gain was KES 2,370.\n• A loss happens when goods sell below cost, e.g. stale mandazi (25% loss).\n• All figures are illustrative (made up).",
      "skills": "• Calculate profit, loss, percentage profit and percentage loss from cost and selling figures (interpretation and inference).\n• Role play buying and selling, record the results in a table and present the findings to peers.\n• Compare items by percentage rather than by shillings alone.",
      "attitudes": "• Peace: respect self and others by listening to others' opinions while comparing predictions and methods.\n• Financial literacy (PCI): appreciate that clubs must check profit before spending it.\n• Value accuracy and honesty when keeping club accounts.",
