        "teacherMoves": "Say: 'Write one question this lesson raised that the cash box and the tourist puzzle still need answered.' WAIT TIME: 15 seconds. Invite 4 learners to read and place their notes. Point to the DQB question about how to plan so the club's money is not less than expected, and ask: 'Which notes help the club plan its Mombasa money?' Move 'Where did the shrinking dollars go?' to the Partly answered column and flag it for Lesson 7. Keep the note: 'Is the deficit of KES 1,515 reduced by changing the sales price or discount?' for Lesson 8.",
        "sensemakingStrategy": "Driving Question Board sorting: classifying questions as answered, partly answered or new keeps learners tracking how each lesson's evidence moves the class toward explaining the phenomenon.",
        "formativeAssessment": "Check that at least 80% of learners contribute a question or answer linked to exchange rates or the budget. Note questions that reveal the buying/selling gap idea (high-quality) versus questions that only ask for another calculation. Tally questions for the Lesson 7 plan."
