        "teacherMoves": "Redraw the model on the board and invite two learners to add boxes. Ask: 'What new cost must a good budget include before the trip?' WAIT TIME: 10 seconds. Cold-call 3 learners for their captions. Say: 'Hold up your notebooks. Which rate column did you write?' Scan the room. Then pose: 'If the club had made the planned KES 5,000 surplus, could it pay?' (Yes, with KES 1,115 to spare.) Close by saying: 'Next lesson we change dollars back and see what happens to Mr Brooks's money.'",
        "sensemakingStrategy": "Cumulative Model Revision: learners add the exchange-rate evidence to a shared model of club money, linking budget, discount, commission, profit and now currency exchange to the single phenomenon of money that appears to shrink.",
        "formativeAssessment": "Observe whether notebooks show: the selling rate 129.50, the product 30 × 129.50 = KES 3,885, and the deficit KES 1,515. Use a thumbs signal (up/sideways/down) to check confidence in choosing a rate column; note learners with sideways or down for a short re-teach using the USD, EUR and GBP rows. Exit ticket: 'KES 8,275 buys how many pounds?' (GBP 50)."
