        "teacherMoves": "Point to the DQB: 'Which of our questions can we answer now? Which are new?' Give each learner one sticky note and 2 minutes of silent writing. WAIT TIME 10 seconds before sharing. Cold-call 4 learners to read and place one note. Ask: 'Is the shrinking dollar the same kind of puzzle as the cash box? How?' Encourage respectful listening: 'Listen to the person speaking, then say what you agree with before you add your idea.' Group similar questions together and label a new column 'Planning for margins'.",
        "sensemakingStrategy": "Driving Question Board: sorting questions into answered and open ones shows learners their growing understanding and keeps the unit's purpose visible. Connecting the two puzzles (cash box and dollars) builds the idea that hidden costs cause the gaps.",
        "formativeAssessment": "Look for questions that go beyond recall, e.g. questions about planning for the margin in the trip budget, or comparing a gap with the discount. Note learners who place a question correctly and give a reason. Check that at least half of the class contribute one note; follow up with those who wrote only 'what is a bureau?'"
